      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-03-11T00:00:00.000Z",
      "title": "Ticop Life Private Limited entered into an agreement to acquire an additional 43.81% stake in Texas Laboratories from Hester Biosciences Limited (BSE:524669) for INR 92 million.",
      "body": "Ticop Life Private Limited entered into an agreement to acquire an additional 43.81% stake in Texas Laboratories from Hester Biosciences Limited (BSE:524669) for INR 92 million on March 5, 2026. A cash consideration of INR 92 million will be paid by Ticop Life Private Limited. The aggregate consideration value of INR 92 million is subject to terms and conditions of agreement. Following the completion Hester Biosciences Limited shareholding will reduce from 54.81% to 11% stake in Texas.\n\nFor the period ending March 31, 2025, Texas Laboratories reported total revenue of INR 285.89 million. As of March 31, 2025, Texas Laboratories reported total common equity of INR 134.17 million.\n\nThe deal has been approved by Hester Biosciences Limited board.\n\nThe transfer of shares shall be completed with",
      "keyDevTypeId": "80",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "d3b94f6b-0a30-451c-9f37-ea88c366d6d1",
      "type": "brief",
      "date": "2026-01-31T20:52:04.000Z",
      "title": "Third quarter 2026 earnings released: EPS: ₹10.94 (vs ₹13.41 in 3Q 2025)",
      "body": "Third quarter 2026 results: EPS: ₹10.94 (down from ₹13.41 in 3Q 2025). Revenue: ₹774.2m (up 9.0% from 3Q 2025). Net income: ₹87.7m (down 25% from 3Q 2025). Profit margin: 11% (down from 16% in 3Q 2025). The decrease in margin was driven by higher expenses. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 14% per year but the company’s share price has fallen by 7% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "BriefActivity"
    },
    {
      "id": "a9be97e6-8ff2-422a-b85a-e371407e77a8",
      "type": "event",
      "date": "2026-01-24T11:37:00.000Z",
      "title": "Hester Biosciences Limited Receives the Manufacturing License from the Food & Drugs Control Administration",
      "body": "Hester Biosciences Limited has received the manufacturing license from the Food & Drugs Control Administration to manufacture and market the Low Pathogenic Avian Influenza Vaccine, Inactivated H9N2 strain for poultry. Low Pathogenic Avian Influenza H9N2 strain has been a persistent challenge in poultry flocks and is known to cause year-round comorbidity, leading to significant economic losses. H9N2 can lead to an irreversible drop in egg production in layers and performance loss in broilers. It can also lead to high mortality in the presence of other infections. This license is a key regulatory milestone in advancing Hester's prevention-led poultry healthcare portfolio. This vaccine has been developed from technology acquired from ICAR-NIHSAD via Agrinnovate India.",
      "keyDevTypeId": "206",
      "source_url": null,
      "raw_subtype": "EventActivity"
    },
